y.com/guides/first-30-days-of-rucking\", \"version_id\": \"e7478e892d0b68e86e3590cf5a6aee352334952687a2aa6cc21c5af1eb937f84\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under the Relevance section this is a training plan for beginner loaded walking, not gear evaluation, and it is explicitly not event preparation, so it does not serve the gear-decision question. Its reliance on editorial starting points and an evidence base that is mostly military and not tested for civilian schedules also fails the Credibility standard for specific claims.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/how-heavy-should-your-ruck-be\", \"version_id\": \"9493cd846697b7ce4138fb6d9363ca50e8390becab392ba0cd1b2ad55ab62c63\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under the Relevance section this is a training-load calculator and progression guide rather than gear evaluation, and its central content (conservative 5-10 lb starting points and body-weight percentages) is editorial guidance that the source itself says is not a threshold. It does not offer gear performance evidence that helps a competitor decide what to carry.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/guides/what-is-rucking-weighted-walking-explained\", \"version_id\": \"4e30a87b3843f861ad970752ef7c31a5e66c382cec6a22c681cbd6891698511f\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under the Relevance section this is an introductory explainer on what rucking is, with no evaluation of specific gear and no new evidence about equipment performance under Mammoth conditions. It duplicates general background and carries affiliate-linked gear mentions without substantive independent testing.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/injuries/rucking-knee-pain\", \"version_id\": \"efaf546f0140dab528ea219954dc01c47943dd1496c66a140ccf8cf559ce6ede\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under the Relevance section this is medical and injury-management content rather than gear evaluation, and it is outside the in-scope gear categories. Its gear mentions (a cushioned shoe and an insole) are promotional affiliate-adjacent asides with no independent test evidence about performance at Mammoth.\", \"piece_ids\": []}\n{\"item_id\": \"feed:https://ruckauthority.com/injuries/rucking-shin-splints-prevention-early-signs-and-recovery-pro\", \"version_id\": \"c326a48b8e179a83b08b5738d25659335affea5b0b8b625a7a0189038beb4ced\", \"decision\": \"reject\", \"reason\": \"Under the Relevance section this is medical injury content about medial tibial stress syndrome rather than gear evaluation, and it falls outside the in-scope gear categories. Its footwear and insole mentions are not supported by product-specific independent testing, so it does not help a competitor decide what to carry.\", \"piece_ids\": []}","ttft_ms":11299,"type":"result","duration_ms":11343,"uuid":"05c91642-38a6-4097-bf6f-aaad0acb23e6","ttft_stream_ms":1080,"time_to_request_ms":297,"first_content_frame_ms":1080,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
